---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="System — PATTERNFORMS"
  description="The PatternForms system: the methodology, Kit of Parts, and IP running through both Studio and Supply arms. Sharpens with every version."
  canonical="https://pattern-forms-website.vercel.app/system"
>
  <div class="pf-page">
    <section class="pf-container">

      <div class="pf-rail-grid">
        <div class="pf-rail">
          <p class="pf-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">05 · SYSTEM</p>
          <div><strong>FUNCTION</strong></div>
          <div>R&amp;D</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 8px;"><strong>DISCIPLINES</strong></div>
          <div>DfMA<br />COMPUTATION<br />PLATFORM LOGIC</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 8px;"><strong>RUNS THROUGH</strong></div>
          <div>STUDIO + SUPPLY</div>
        </div>

        <div class="pf-system-body">
          <p class="pf-body">
            Where Studio and Supply synthesise — elevating the products and projects we make for you.
          </p>
          <p class="pf-body">
            This is our R&amp;D frontier: bridging the gap between Design for Manufacture and Assembly
            (DfMA) of a Kit of Parts, and the real, unique requirements of your project.
          </p>
          <p class="pf-body">
            Systemised building is still new ground in Australia — and the world, really. We are
            interested in one idea: that a whole project can be answered by a system stacked by design
            inputs, parts, data, and the tools that tie them together.
          </p>
          <p class="pf-body">
            In pursuing this, we borrow terms and practices from established industries — automotive,
            heavy industry, manufacturing — in our purpose to productise the major aspects of building
            assemblies.
          </p>

          <!-- PILLARS -->
          <div class="pf-pillars">
            <p class="pf-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">SOME PILLARS OF INTEREST</p>
            <div class="pf-pillars-grid">
              <div class="pf-pillar">
                <h4 class="pf-pillar-head">PLATFORM LOGIC</h4>
                <p class="pf-pillar-body">The fewest parts that produce the most variety.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="pf-pillar">
                <h4 class="pf-pillar-head">PHYSICAL RATIONALISATION</h4>
                <p class="pf-pillar-body">Fewer components, cleaner connections, simpler assembly.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="pf-pillar">
                <h4 class="pf-pillar-head">DATA BACKBONE</h4>
                <p class="pf-pillar-body">One source of truth, from design through to the bill of materials.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="pf-pillar">
                <h4 class="pf-pillar-head">COMPUTATION</h4>
                <p class="pf-pillar-body">Software that executes the system with speed and accuracy.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="pf-pillar">
                <h4 class="pf-pillar-head">COMMERCIALISATION</h4>
                <p class="pf-pillar-body">Building delivered as a product, refined version over version — not reinvented each project.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p class="pf-body">
            We will keep the how to ourselves for now. What makes us unusual in Melbourne is that
            we speak both languages of construction and manufacturing.
          </p>
          <p class="pf-body">
            If any of this resonates, we would be glad to talk.{' '}
            <a href="mailto:interest@patternforms.au" class="pf-inline-link">interest@patternforms.au</a>
          </p>
          <p class="pf-body" style="color: var(--pf-grey-60);">
            PS. The system does not replace the design response of a project, nor control project
            aesthetics. We believe in individual and crafted building projects — just ones that enjoy
            predictable and effective components under the hood ;)
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .pf-system-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 36px;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .pf-pillars {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .pf-pillars-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .pf-pillars-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .pf-pillars-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  }

  .pf-pillar {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .pf-pillar-head {
    font-family: var(--pf-font-body);
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.10em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--pf-ink);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .pf-pillar-body {
    font-family: var(--pf-font-body);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--pf-grey-60);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .pf-inline-link {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--pf-grey-30);
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    transition: color 200ms var(--pf-ease-snap), border-color 200ms var(--pf-ease-snap);
  }
  .pf-inline-link:hover {
    color: var(--pf-terra);
    border-bottom-color: var(--pf-terra);
  }
</style>
